# Scheduled jobs — supercronic, container TZ=America/New_York, so every time
# below is ET and matches the times the command files state directly.
#
# The minutes are deliberately off :00/:15/:30. Every scheduler on the planet
# fires on those marks; :17 and :22 sidestep the herd at both the Schwab and
# Anthropic APIs for no cost.
#
# Labor Day 2026-09-07 is NOT special-cased. /deep-research §A and
# get_market_hours no-op it, at the cost of one wasted run. That is deliberate:
# a date hard-coded into a schedule file is a date that silently stops matching
# its rule — the exact defect commit 8f2171c removed from the dispatch prompt.
#
# Every job goes through scheduled-run.sh, which owns locking, the ET window
# guard, logging and the heartbeat. Nothing calls `claude` directly.

# --- research ------------------------------------------------------------
17 8  * * 1-5   /app/scripts/scheduled-run.sh preopen
22 16 * * 1-5   /app/scripts/scheduled-run.sh postclose
40 7  * * 6     /app/scripts/scheduled-run.sh weekly-universe

# --- watchdogs (Phase 3) --------------------------------------------------
5  7  * * *     /app/scripts/token-watchdog.sh
35 9  * * 1-5   /app/scripts/job-deadman.sh

# --- deployment (Phase 1b) ------------------------------------------------
# 18:30 ET: after postclose has finished, long before the next preopen. Never
# inside 09:15-16:15 — a restart there drops any pending Discord approval,
# whose state is in-memory and process-local (approvals/codemap.md).
30 18 * * 1-5   /app/scripts/deploy.sh
